<title>USA: Jacor buys four Idaho radio stations.</title>
<headline>Jacor buys four Idaho radio stations.</headline>
<dateline>COVINGTON, Ky. 1997-06-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Jacor Communications Inc said it agreed to buy four radio stations in Idaho from Lartigue Multimedia Inc for $3.4 million.</p>
<p>The stations are KID-FM and KID-AM in Pocatello, and KPKY-FM and KWIK-AM in Idaho Falls, the company said in a news release Friday.</p>
<p>Jacor owns, operates or provides programming for 149 radio stations in 32 U.S. broadcast areas.</p>
